# Backend conventions

- Keep domain behaviour in focused services and modules; controllers validate, authorize, document, and delegate.
- Use dependency injection and existing domain modules instead of new global helpers or duplicate services.
- Validate all external input with DTOs; never trust TypeScript types at runtime.
- Enforce authorization centrally with guards and re-check ownership in service queries.
- Put multi-record state transitions in transactions and enforce concurrency invariants in PostgreSQL constraints or conditional writes.
- Never hold a database transaction open during an external network call.
- Queue jobs must be idempotent, retry-safe, observable, bounded, and recoverable after worker restarts.
- Use Prisma CLI-generated migrations. Document rollout, backfill, compatibility, and rollback considerations.
- Avoid unsafe raw SQL. Parameterize justified raw queries and test them against PostgreSQL.
- Log structured identifiers and outcomes without credentials, cookies, tokens, personal data, or provider secrets.
- Keep public response DTOs explicit; do not leak Prisma records by accident.
